---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { beta, contacts, mailto } from '../config/site';
---

<Base
  title="Help and support"
  description="Help with Math Dragons: joining the beta, devices, resetting progress, and how to reach us."
  path="/support"
>
  <h1>Help and support</h1>

  <div class="card highlight">
    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      For questions, bug reports or feedback, email
      <a href={mailto(contacts.support, 'Math Dragons help')}>{contacts.support}</a>. We aim to
      respond within 48 hours.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Please include your device model and system version if something isn't working.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>What ages is Math Dragons for?</dt>
    <dd>Kids ages 5 to 12. It practices addition, subtraction, multiplication and division facts.</dd>

    <dt>Which devices does it work on?</dt>
    <dd>
      iPhone and iPad with iOS or iPadOS 15 or later, and Android phones and tablets with Android 7.0
      or later.
    </dd>

    <dt>How do I join the beta?</dt>
    <dd>
      Follow the steps on the <a href="/#join">home page</a>. iPhone and iPad use Apple's TestFlight
      app. Android uses a Google tester group and Google Play.
    </dd>

    <dt>Android says "App not available." What now?</dt>
    <dd>
      Make sure the Google account signed in to the Play Store is the same one that joined the
      tester group. Then wait a few minutes and open the tester page again, in Chrome.
    </dd>

    <dt>Does it need the internet?</dt>
    <dd>No. Math Dragons works offline.</dd>

    <dt>Are there ads or purchases?</dt>
    <dd>
      No ads. There are no purchases right now: everything is free during the beta. Paid features
      are planned for the full release. Everyone in the beta gets the full unlock free when Math
      Dragons launches. It's our thank-you for joining.
    </dd>

    <dt>What does the app do with my child's information?</dt>
    <dd>
      Nothing leaves the app. The app collects no data and has no accounts, and we never receive
      your child's progress. It stays on your device (and in your device's own backup, if you use
      one). See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for details.
    </dd>

    <dt>How do I reset my child's progress?</dt>
    <dd>
      On Android, open Settings, then Apps, then Math Dragons, then Storage (or Storage &amp; cache),
      and tap Clear storage (Clear data on some phones). On iPhone or iPad, delete the app and
      install it again. Either way, all progress and settings on the device are erased. A device
      backup may still hold an older copy.
    </dd>

    <dt>Can more than one child use it on the same device?</dt>
    <dd>
      Right now the app has one player profile per device. Siblings sharing a device share the same
      dragon and progress.
    </dd>

    <dt>I reset or reinstalled the app. Do I still get the beta thank-you?</dt>
    <dd>
      Yes. Email <a href={mailto(contacts.support, 'Math Dragons beta thank-you')}>{contacts.support}</a>
      and we'll make sure you get the full unlock at launch.
    </dd>

    <dt>How do I leave the beta?</dt>
    <dd>
      On iPhone or iPad, open the TestFlight app, choose Math Dragons, and tap Stop Testing (deleting
      the app alone doesn't leave the beta). On Android, open
      <a href={beta.playOptIn}>the tester page</a> and choose Leave the program, then uninstall.
    </dd>

    <dt>The app crashed or isn't working right.</dt>
    <dd>
      Close and reopen the app, then try restarting the device. If it keeps happening, email
      <a href={mailto(contacts.support, 'Math Dragons bug report')}>{contacts.support}</a> with what
      happened and your device model and system version.
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>About the app</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>Developer</dt>
    <dd>{contacts.developer}</dd>
    <dt>Ages</dt>
    <dd>5 to 12</dd>
    <dt>Ads</dt>
    <dd>None</dd>
    <dt>Internet required</dt>
    <dd>No</dd>
    <dt>Price</dt>
    <dd>Free during the beta</dd>
  </dl>
</Base>
